v><div data-rid="59de9415-664b-44d0-ab94-12d3ec8ce13e" data-cart-count="" class="r-j0oqys alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><br></p></span></div></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="559195a5-66b7-4168-ba8f-8394a7a0b0ab" class="r-1uv2elu"><div data-rid="9ca10be2-9d03-4656-baa9-205faca13ea0" class="r-z44kxy"><div data-rid="99bce1cd-dcef-40c4-8cb2-917e9960ddbe" class="r-qv6z8s"><div data-rid="ab5cb273-0026-44d0-b041-5d7e5982ab81" class="r-sy3wz2"><div data-rid="5ef073ce-7f2e-4ead-a88f-722d9735f98b" class="r-37kwbh alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>6 Signs Your Body Is Running a Deficit & Coffee Just Hides It.</p></span></div><div data-rid="1117cfb6-0940-4df1-911a-7db896d21444" class="r-1rjhtnv alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Caffeine masks the signal. It doesn't fix the source. Most people are running daily deficits in the exact nutrients that drive real energy production, cognitive function, and physical recovery. <strong>Here are six reasons coffee is hiding what's actually going on underneath.</strong></p></span></div></div><div data-rid="273b2ec0-86ab-4554-b513-e27d7c8cfd9e" class="r-zlh5xo"><div data-rid="16f0b087-c7b9-41fb-a0f9-fd7fd824a56b" class="r-1uaumsr"><picture data-rid="7ad69e1b-e5ee-4bb7-b66c-854c0c118cd2" class="r-z7z57f"><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/96c84196-cac8-42df-8c1a-53e4013dca0f?width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/96c84196-cac8-42df-8c1a-53e4013dca0f?width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/96c84196-cac8-42df-8c1a-53e4013dca0f?width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/96c84196-cac8-42df-8c1a-53e4013dca0f" class="r-t5oqri" loading="eager"/></picture></div></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="adf804dc-695e-4a26-9b53-9478d4dfd33f" class="r-ive57g"><div data-rid="484e0c09-0643-4052-bc79-10b842e8dc1b" class="r-1lu1rbg"><div data-rid="b095e054-cb1e-4d1a-9ddb-5ddc33077ec0" class="r-33h1hq"><div data-rid="07f51695-4e33-435a-910b-708cb976b2da" class="r-1mg7wsh"><picture data-rid="ecf86584-ee5b-4080-90fd-1971ed1d44f0" class="r-1d22546"><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/465ada07-66cb-49db-984f-4ceae8e8dab5?width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/465ada07-66cb-49db-984f-4ceae8e8dab5?width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/465ada07-66cb-49db-984f-4ceae8e8dab5?width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/465ada07-66cb-49db-984f-4ceae8e8dab5" class="r-1z0p4z6" loading="eager"/></picture></div><div data-rid="ab47fc71-5c74-4f85-97be-57c7bbec7c74" class="r-1sx1j9e"><div data-rid="09411e20-defa-45ef-b547-6ccc7a6f2877" class="r-jxtgs6"><div data-rid="1637f48c-91ef-4ef0-8296-6063ae51e6fc" class="r-13631q alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>SIGN #1</p></span></div><div data-rid="af69ab82-4ce0-4fc5-8cf7-a8cb3d2c63de" class="r-u0t5rn alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Your muscles are running on empty.</p></span></div><div data-rid="319148a4-1ad1-4b8e-aca9-f32328026be1" class="r-qp6ua8 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Your body stores energy as ATP — and every high-output day depletes it. Without the right nutritional support, your muscles spend more to produce less. <strong>Coffee tells your brain to ignore the signal and so the deficit keeps building.</strong></p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="9934e5d0-2425-4710-8f9c-4d35695373ab" class="r-61gkfz"><div data-rid="284c2ab7-cbdd-4db2-85e7-e50f94a8215c" class="r-15ldpys"><picture data-rid="d6501316-9505-47e8-9d9f-383dca430344" class="r-55lkj5"><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/c24067f2-06fe-465d-b7bd-9d5c7a40a564?width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/c24067f2-06fe-465d-b7bd-9d5c7a40a564?width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/c24067f2-06fe-465d-b7bd-9d5c7a40a564?width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/c24067f2-06fe-465d-b7bd-9d5c7a40a564" class="r-17s0y6b" loading="eager"/></picture></div><div data-rid="43e3e0c8-3498-40a4-b766-52ad2f3963fe" class="r-9ckkkp"><div data-rid="3e7dc65f-9d2b-4c9f-af5d-1d404e0e718d" class="r-148f4iw"><div data-rid="6f4c6ffc-041a-4d2e-af32-764b51ddfe0f" class="r-694d2r alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>SIGN #2</p></span></div><div data-rid="61316a4c-43d0-4b6c-a792-772044117771" class="r-1hs9oqr alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Every cup of coffee gives you less than the last one did.</p></span></div><div data-rid="9a4e839e-c47f-4d52-8091-4e6daa84bec2" class="r-1wa93y3 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p><strong>Caffeine blocks fatigue receptors but doesn't remove the fatigue.</strong> Adenosine keeps stacking underneath — which is why cup three does less than cup one. You're not running on energy. You're borrowing against a reserve that never gets refilled.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="624f0e1c-66cc-4af2-9ed7-098320bca6e5" class="r-1lwoaq9"><div data-rid="f53d1978-27ed-42b0-bf44-4563383aba54" class="r-5vqabg"><picture data-rid="6f29f282-ff72-48d0-9de7-7d97433cb492" class="r-e75u89"><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/71074ca5-4b07-440e-b87a-cabbd23f3095?width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/71074ca5-4b07-440e-b87a-cabbd23f3095?width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/71074ca5-4b07-440e-b87a-cabbd23f3095?width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/71074ca5-4b07-440e-b87a-cabbd23f3095" class="r-1ygaba9" loading="eager"/></picture></div><div data-rid="0e5857c5-2cfa-4e6d-9952-e9e7f93201ea" class="r-sg6k4w"><div data-rid="e60a462d-f1a4-4adc-911e-281d87fd9e31" class="r-jiscmr"><div data-rid="4ff84f36-6f36-491d-a0ef-64d9d8645e8f" class="r-8grj24 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>SIGN #3</p></span></div><div data-rid="d7c75b25-6511-40ab-8174-8bb43a41085c" class="r-108ksy7 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>You wake up feeling behind before the day even starts.</p></span></div><div data-rid="2ad42395-49d5-4d47-913a-dcc3abd601c7" class="r-zbn1b5 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Recovery depends on specific amino acids and minerals that are chronically under-consumed in most diets. When they aren't available, your body deprioritizes repair to keep you functional the next day. <strong>Coffee and energy drinks accelerate cortisol production, which interfere with your body’s natural repair process.</strong></p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="4f55bd7c-7171-418b-bf54-60e24b39f81e" class="r-gfb003"><div data-rid="e157767a-5971-4333-bfcf-e5c7a8ec7a1d" class="r-f6h21p"><picture data-rid="544115bd-d5e3-41a6-b344-c6f40d04ed5a" class="r-15qledy"><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/b679caae-0cd7-44c3-b36b-625785b83c29?width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/b679caae-0cd7-44c3-b36b-625785b83c29?width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/b679caae-0cd7-44c3-b36b-625785b83c29?width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/b679caae-0cd7-44c3-b36b-625785b83c29" class="r-x097go" loading="eager"/></picture></div><div data-rid="06472e5c-89ce-4bda-9bf4-5e492392b02f" class="r-1ltxn7p"><div data-rid="a5f95a9b-3e29-48e1-bb85-512a7a2cc1de" class="r-2ensj1"><div data-rid="47c924fd-5262-4639-a195-dc8f80108bba" class="r-1nfmjqq alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>SIGN #4</p></span></div><div data-rid="b24f9be2-3bcd-4219-8980-e5557264992d" class="r-1uo1k3l alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>That 10am fog isn't tiredness. It's a chemistry problem.</p></span></div><div data-rid="155f73e6-9109-4ee5-97f6-23a1630edde0" data-listing-list="" class="r-uogwf5 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Sustained focus depletes the neurotransmitters behind attention and clarity. <br></p><ul><li><p><strong>Caffeine </strong>makes your brain run hotter on fewer resources and <strong>doesn’t fix the actual shortage.</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Energy drinks </strong>add B vitamins but <strong>don't address neurotransmitter depletion</strong>.</p></li></ul><p><br>The fog at hour ten is a chemistry problem, not a willpower problem.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="c53c4a5d-eb88-4d52-bd1a-8c552e84f1ca" class="r-10757on"><div data-rid="ead8a2a3-e2e8-4283-8d2d-487a861c77bb" class="r-pd0rgs"><picture data-rid="15bf0e24-09e5-4d13-98cb-639b158a1a7f" class="r-8l38ch"><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/70567dc1-768a-4a1a-a954-c546c5729fed?width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/70567dc1-768a-4a1a-a954-c546c5729fed?width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/70567dc1-768a-4a1a-a954-c546c5729fed?width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/70567dc1-768a-4a1a-a954-c546c5729fed" alt="A diagram comparing unhealthy and healthy cell energy cycles, with a person riding a motorcycle in the background." class="r-1cren7t" loading="eager"/></picture></div><div data-rid="f0bf9485-cd0c-4559-9f1d-b4fcc760337d" class="r-11mpcy4"><div data-rid="df64910e-b874-444b-bb2c-ae3cbf9f157c" class="r-qa09xv"><div data-rid="4a6136aa-5294-41fe-9083-ccb69a35e21e" class="r-rphs80 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>SIGN #5</p></span></div><div data-rid="eb8f094e-8c43-4a8a-bede-2a879d26cd6d" class="r-18t76k8 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>You're eating enough but your energy still doesn't show up.</p></span></div><div data-rid="81dff99b-5ba1-4d10-9017-562fb238493c" data-listing-list="" class="r-15eain3 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Food needs specific nutrients to convert into usable energy inside your mitochondria. When those are missing, fuel sits at the door. <br><br><strong>Caffeine bypasses this entirely — which is why the energy feels artificial and drops hard.</strong></p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="e0b4a3f0-263f-491a-9ce7-b2a8d553b262" class="r-1bshkbx"><div data-rid="48eba9c3-0c12-41e7-ba61-9b2b9009a7eb" class="r-fflu06"><picture data-rid="b62fa723-b846-4dc2-902e-18eeb3f8a3cf" class="r-834rei"><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/825d8a5c-c7bb-4f7b-b029-af80ece1b3d8?width=820" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/825d8a5c-c7bb-4f7b-b029-af80ece1b3d8?width=1024" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/825d8a5c-c7bb-4f7b-b029-af80ece1b3d8?width=1800" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/825d8a5c-c7bb-4f7b-b029-af80ece1b3d8" alt="A man in a brown beanie looks away from a to-do list with &#x27;Morning Routine&#x27; checked off." class="r-1hvtvz9" loading="eager"/></picture></div><div data-rid="9a23c894-be4f-4c2e-9370-110396c4ef30" class="r-372uid"><div data-rid="779e8503-270a-44ac-a136-e2362ab5a4ef" class="r-19ei5rs"><div data-rid="ce4723f1-eed9-4233-9499-b52b917f171f" class="r-17t36sr alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>SIGN #6</p></span></div><div data-rid="8626c1e7-b418-4c3a-b637-302d2c35d7c4" class="r-aksgh4 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>You've normalized feeling low energy. That's the problem.</p></span></div><div data-rid="0d4573d7-3437-4259-8602-683fbde0a189" data-listing-list="" class="r-1hvji68 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>When tired becomes your baseline, you stop looking for a fix. You reach for another coffee and call it fine. Fine isn't optimized. The energy, focus, and output you're missing isn't gone — it's been masked.</p></span></div></div></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="ac11bc1a-88e5-4b75-b3fc-dabeb209aa63" class="r-14fzo0o"><div class="r-11lw2et" data-rid="1"><div data-rid="cc91ae55-4586-4480-84ad-c2eb0f3def42" class="r-1gy96kw"><div data-rid="39e87b1c-1a40-4bce-9fec-594a5fd8739d" class="r-cpzg71"><div data-rid="405c77c3-2436-4f30-be92-0d4a1ee0ef26" class="r-f66183 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><h2>One scoop replaces all of it.</h2></span></div><div data-rid="3c26947e-3cab-488b-a91a-9fe7025a210b" class="r-1vsh6jc alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Not because your diet is broken. Because the demands of your day are higher than any diet was designed to meet. Meet Every Damn Day, your all-in-one daily performance support.</p></span></div><div data-rid="b4436f71-4a37-4a3a-9c1d-6a943226258a" class="r-w8iwt1"><div data-rid="888c1011-3715-49dc-8b47-dded61ab022b" class="r-jzpfik" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed"><div data-rid="9abeecf3-e788-4de0-bfae-c1a40b884751" aria-controls="replo-:R7dj2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-1ty5kr7"><div data-rid="f660adeb-962d-4eec-b61e-528304e729ab" class="r-dq07k3 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>creatine monohydrate</p></span></div><div data-rid="9bab0416-9a0b-4085-abf1-c5703dc7fa2c" class="r-1xu5y88"><picture data-rid="a1935b14-f631-4bd8-89a1-9f4b8104a9d4" class="r-17ksp0k"><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/fee7fe1d-5c50-40b6-b06b-aff262d55084?width=40" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/fee7fe1d-5c50-40b6-b06b-aff262d55084?width=48" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/fee7fe1d-5c50-40b6-b06b-aff262d55084?width=48" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/fee7fe1d-5c50-40b6-b06b-aff262d55084" class="r-k1bchp" loading="lazy"/></picture><div data-rid="2b739444-a9c2-4678-95ee-268d2d786edc" class="r-uye2hg alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Power</p></span></div></div><div data-rid="147cb313-c755-48db-9c47-a9cd2e441635" class="r-o7a2ml"><div data-rid="b53d2a84-d2fb-4a88-93a0-22ebdfc6b039" class="r-163pfd8 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>5g</p></span></div><div data-rid="88e9b1e8-a9a0-48b5-921f-a028f50d29b4" class="r-1ojq0vm"><span style="display:contents"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="feather feather-chevron-down" style="fill: none;stroke: currentColor;width: var(--rsw, 100%);height: auto" role="img" aria-label="Collapse/Expand"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"></polyline></svg></span></div></div></div><div class="replo-animated" hidden="" id="replo-:R7dj2:"><div data-rid="7f7f27a0-9cef-4cea-b01e-e6eefb2ccaff" class="r-ul44sq"><div data-rid="86d04a57-7e5f-4255-8ba8-3b78f3f7259d" class="r-1ot9715 alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>Clinically proven to boost strength, muscle power, and recovery by increasing ATP - your body's primary energy source for high-intensity performance. Creatine also enhances brain energy metabolism, supporting sharper thinking, better memory, and improved mental performance under stress.</p></span></div></div></div></div><div data-rid="1fd9c38d-6d93-4237-94ba-d6511ee03b93" class="r-gc3vd6" data-replo-collapsible="true" data-state="closed"><div data-rid="7443f592-6700-40d5-ae52-dfebf9f6c52a" aria-controls="replo-:Rbdj2:" tabindex="0" role="button" class="r-7peq1s"><div data-rid="4216a709-c005-4a03-aec3-71f0d988de22" class="r-18rxp0m alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><p>l-citrulline</p></span></div><div data-rid="964d1539-6e1c-43a6-a104-9293b64b9f95" class="r-hw3xt3"><picture data-rid="68814615-1eae-407c-83ce-cb80098772a7" class="r-11jci06"><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/fee7fe1d-5c50-40b6-b06b-aff262d55084?width=40" media="(max-width: 640px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/fee7fe1d-5c50-40b6-b06b-aff262d55084?width=48" media="(min-width: 641px) and (max-width: 1024px)"/><source srcSet="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4610-914e-30c6f6c7f5fc/fee7fe1d-5c50-40b6-b06b-aff262d55084?width=48" media="(min-width: 1025px) and (max-width: 2400px)"/><img src="https://assets.replocdn.com/projects/8a734d7d-8e00-4